⚡🇨🇾🇬🇧🇮🇷 A British man has been arrested on espionage charges at a British military base in Cyprus on behalf of the Iranian army.

According to the BBC, Rashad Sultanov, 44, from Islington in north London, is accused of conducting "hostile surveillance" on RAF Akrotiri and sharing information with the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps. Sultanov, who also holds Azerbaijani citizenship, was arrested by Cypriot police on July 17 and is in custody awaiting extradition proceedings.

